Selawik -- the face of the "aero" desktop theme (~/.config/themes/aero/).

Selawik is Microsoft's open-source fallback for Segoe UI: same metrics and
proportions as the Windows 7 / Vista UI face, under a free licence. Segoe UI
itself cannot be used here (its licence is Windows-only), so this is the
closest legal match. It covers Latin only (348 glyphs, no arrows, no CJK), so
the theme lists IBM Plex Sans right after it and fontconfig falls back per
glyph; its figures are tabular by default (every digit 1104/1153 units wide),
so the clock and the rates do not jitter without a "tnum" feature.

Source:   https://github.com/microsoft/Selawik  (official Microsoft repo)
Release:  1.01, 2015-12-08
          https://github.com/microsoft/Selawik/releases/download/1.01/Selawik_Release.zip
          sha256 3f62c51e05e3b5a1e6241cf92a371f0be2ea1183aa87b30718bbd40832a8d423
Files:    the five .ttf from that zip, unmodified:
          selawkl (Light) selawksl (Semilight) selawk (Regular)
          selawksb (Semibold) selawkb (Bold)
Licence:  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (LICENSE.txt next to this file, taken from
          the repo's master branch -- the release zip ships no licence file).
          Personal use, embedding and redistribution allowed; the fonts may
          not be sold on their own; "Selawik" is a Reserved Font Name, so a
          modified copy would have to be renamed.
Installed: 2026-10-17, user-level only (fc-cache -f ~/.local/share/fonts).
